6	 * the same `gh` call; `scripts/resolve_orchestrator_parent.ts` issued its own
7	 * GraphQL query for GitHub's native sub-issue `parent` field and fell back to the
8	 * tag. Nothing recorded why one of the three had the richer rule.
9	 *
10	 * The richer rule is the right one and is now everyone's. GitHub's own parent
11	 * link is authoritative when it exists, and the tag is what Atomaton writes itself
12	 * -- an issue created by `create_issue` carries the tag whether or not the native
13	 * link was established, and `addSubIssue` is best-effort.
14	 *
15	 * Not `issueLinks`, which answers a much larger question: it pulls fifty children
16	 * and fifty pull requests, and every caller here wants one number.
